==Trivia==
*He appears to be based on Satan, who is the "Emperor of Darkness". One of his variants, [[Satan Claus]], even has "Satan" in his name.
**He may specifically be inspired by [[wikia:ghostsngoblins:Lucifer|Great Demon Lord Lucifer]] of the ''[[wikipedia:Ghosts 'n Goblins|Ghosts 'n Goblins]]'' series, who is also a red, nude, muscular final boss that spends the fight on a throne and attacks by pointing his index fingers. [[Galactic Overseer Nyandam]] could further reference said attack.
*Despite lacking any visual similarities, Nyandam is quite possibly a reference to the Michelin Man [[wikipedia:Bibendum|Bibendum]], mascot of the Michelin tyre company. In Japanese, ''Bibendum'' is pronounced ''Bibandamu'' (ビバンダム), while ''Nyandam'' is ''Ni~yandamu'' (ニャンダム). Furthermore, Bibendum was initially conceived as a [https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/8/88/Michelin_Poster_1898.jpg regal figure] holding a glass of beer and exclaiming the Latin phrase ''Nunc est bibendum'' ("Now is the time to drink"), while Nyandam ironically cannot drink, and instead only pretends he could.
*His Japanese description may have foreshadowed [[Infernal Tyrant Nyandam]], as it says that Nyandam merely dyed his body [[:Category:Red Enemies|Red]] in order to feel drunk, while Infernal Tyrant Nyandam is a non-Red form of Nyandam that he had 560,000 years ago.
*His Japanese description and red dye reference [[wikipedia:Alcohol flush reaction|alcohol flush reaction]], also known as Asian red face glow.
*In the Korean version, the glass is stated to be filled with grape jelly rather than coffee jelly.
*His name was changed from "Nyandum" to "Nyandam" between the two English versions. "Nyandum" was either one of many typos or mistranslations from [[Battle Cats (Removed Game)|Battle Cats]], or a deliberate naming choice intended to make the Bibendum reference more obvious.
*He appears during [[Benevolent Souma (Uber Rare Cat)|Souma & Cat]]'s attack animation.
*In [[Yuru-i GeGeGe no Kitarou: Youkai Dotabata Daisensou]], [[wikia:gegegenokitaro:Kagami-Jijii|Kagami-Jijii]] used an attack strikingly similar to Dark Emperor Nyandam's.
*[[The Face]], Dark Emperor Nyandam and [[Teacher Bun Bun]] all share the same amount of health: 99,999. However, Nyandam only has [[Soul Leasing|one unbuffed appearance]], and Teacher Bun Bun is always fought at 400% or more.
*He is the first enemy to debut at a strength magnification above 100%, being buffed to 150% in [[Empire of Cats]] Chapter 2's [[Moon (Empire of Cats)|Moon/Iriomote]] stage.

